    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13209" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēportātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		deporto (rare), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a carrying</i> or <i>conveying away, a
				transportation</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i><span class="en">Cato R. R. 144, 3</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>a perpetual banishment, transportation, deportation,
				exile</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 48, 13, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">48, 22, 6 al.</span></i>;
			cf. deporto, <i>no.</i> II. B.</div>
